WEBVTT

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.080
Damn.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.040
I wish they'd quit pounding down on us already.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.130
How's a man supposed to enjoy a meal?

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:39.050
We're hardly in any position to complain,

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.340
compared to the ones on the front lines...

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.840
We're at a serious positional 
disadvantage here.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.610
There's more to it than that.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.320
Their firing range is incredible, too.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.580
Is it the new chrars, do you think?

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:57.570
Likely.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:01.580
They're probably mounted on 
all the Order's theurgears.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:12.280
Is that the power of the new chrars?

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.470
You think they're installing one
every new model they make?

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:19.470
Just goes to show how desperate they are.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.110
This is a critical point for them, after all.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:24.060
It is for us, too.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.850
If we break through here, 
we'll be able to rush their capital.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.470
All right, get in position.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.450
Our turn's up.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.240
Roger that.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.120
I take it back.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.780
We'll be waiting a little longer.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.960
They've changed the plan, I'd wager.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:46.000
The plan?

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.450
The stalemate's gone on too long.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:51.000
Someone's out of patience.

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:55.010
Chief of Staff Fleet has arrived.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.190
The Price of Smiles

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.190
<i>The Price of Smiles</i>

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:34.400
<b><i>The Night of the Squad</i></b>

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:32.230
In order to break out of 
our current deadlock,

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:35.230
we'll run a flying column operation.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:40.690
We're sure that the enemy's encamped in 
a city on this tongue-shaped plateau,

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:45.240
but from our position below, 
we can't confirm their precise location.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:46.440
However...

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:52.890
A recon unit made it behind their camp 
through the forest to their south.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.630
They took this photograph.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.520
The bridge here hasn't been collapsed.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.850
The flying column will cross that bridge 
to strike their camp from the rear.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:02.910
It will consist of...

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:06.610
Hirsch Squad.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:07.580
Sir!

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.950
Schaff Squad.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:09.640
Sir!

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.440
And Buerger Squad.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:12.140
Sir!

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:17.340
Huey!

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:18.770
That you, Huey?

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:21.030
Stella! And Lily!

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:23.250
Hey! Long time no see!

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:24.490
Friends of yours?

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:28.040
We were stationed together in 
our early days, that's all.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.220
Hey, don't be like that.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.240
We really looked out for you guys!

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:35.250
Yeah, you taught us a few things, 
that's for sure!

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:38.470
I see you've made yourselves 
a bit useful, at least.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:42.130
I was worried, at first, 
all you greenhorns together...

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:45.380
I see you haven't changed a bit, though.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:49.640
You always were smiling like 
nothing could scare you.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.390
Are you here for our next mission?

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.400
Yeah, we're in the Hirsch Squad right now.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.570
The fighting's about to get serious, they say.

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:58.850
Even more than now, that is.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:00.650
Well, see you around. Try not to die.

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.250
No worries about that.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.400
If there's one thing I've got, 
it's stupid good luck.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.850
You're still such a brat.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.990
They really put you through 
the wringer back then, huh?

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:16.370
They did a lot to show 
us the ropes, actually.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.830
They just like to talk nasty.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.000
Look nasty, too.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.000
Is everyone here?

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.530
Get inside. I'll explain the plan.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:29.520
Under cover of night, we'll circle 
around this way, heading south.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.830
Once we pass the tributary on 
our right, we'll head west.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:34.380
The bridge will be just ahead.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.900
Our squad will be the vanguard.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:41.650
What if we're sighted before 
we reach our target?

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.540
That's already been taken into account.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:47.780
If we're seen, we can still be 
useful by creating a diversion.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.590
"Play the good little decoy," eh?

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:53.790
If you don't like the idea, do your 
best to make sure we aren't seen.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.880
What she said, more or less.

00:05:56.590 --> 00:06:00.150
From the bridge, we'll pass through the forest 
and confirm the enemy camp's location.

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:02.710
If we succeed, we'll contact 
the main force with a flare.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.700
Once the shelling begins, we'll rush them 
from behind to throw them off balance

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.300
while our main force pours into their camp.

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:12.120
You really think it'll be that easy?

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.780
They'll have sentries all over that forest.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.510
The concentration of forces on the front line

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:20.090
suggests their rear guard 
will be undermanned.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:22.560
The plan's a lot of wishful thinking.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.840
We'll kick this off at 0100 hours.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:29.820
We'll be navigating a forest at night. 
Take care that you don't get separated.

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:32.130
I'm sure we'll be fine.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:35.700
As long as no one decides 
to run off on his own...

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.310
No need to worry about that.

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:43.220
This isn't some cushy operation 
I can trust you to handle without me.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.710
Take those words to heart.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.340
Still can't stand that guy.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:54.470
We still don't know why 
he joined our squad, either.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:57.770
I think... it might have been for money.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:58.670
For money?

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:02.650
I saw him make a money 
transfer back at camp earlier.

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:04.100
I was right nearby.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:07.320
That's not so weird. 
He's probably got family.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:09.820
Or a girlfriend.

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:12.890
But it was quite a significant amount.

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:16.790
Even the accountant ended up 
asking who it was for.

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.440
What did he say in response?

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.820
He said...

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:25.360
"I have a battalion's worth of little 
birds waiting for their feed."

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:27.810
What the hell does that mean?

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:30.960
It means he's got a lot of stamina, 
if you get what I'm saying.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.120
Yeah, yeah...

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:33.090
It must be really something, huh?

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:33.880
What?

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:34.900
You know what.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:38.120
Hey, Lily, hey!

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.100
You get what he meant?

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:57.830
<i>The tributary's in view on the right.</i>

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.350
We'll go straight for two more klicks,

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:03.040
then cross the river and start heading west.

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:16.660
Once we're over this hill, 
the bridge should be in sight.

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:21.100
What is it?

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.540
Signal the squads behind us to stop.

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:26.060
You see that?

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:29.320
A... theurgear?

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:31.790
Looks like scrap to me.

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:33.320
It's a makeshift pillbox.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.530
They're hidden inside, keeping watch.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:37.610
Should we blast 'em?

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:38.710
Make it fast and thorough.

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:39.980
Don't let them report back.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:41.920
Any other theurgears around?

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:43.580
None.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.590
Right, 12 degrees.

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:00.850
Range, 203.

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:05.620
Angle of elevation, 17... no, 18 degrees.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:07.990
<i>Okay, I'm on it. Come on back.</i>

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:30.930
Okay, let's head back.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:33.500
Roger that!

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:41.560
Lily!

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:57.610
Ow!

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:01.350
Is it the leg?

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.620
It doesn't appear to be broken, but...

00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:06.230
Well, count yourself lucky.

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:08.990
It would've been worse if my 
theurgear hadn't soaked the blast.

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:10.840
You call this lucky?!

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:13.580
If you hadn't sprung their trap, 
this wouldn't haveー

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:14.340
Ow, ow, ow!

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:18.530
Well, it's clear you're a 
lucky bastard, at least.

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:21.460
You'd have eaten a direct hit 
if you hadn't slipped first.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:21.840
That again?

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:25.100
But this looks pretty bad, doesn't it?

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.110
I'm fine.

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:28.600
I've trained for...

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:31.520
Were either of the other 
squads assigned a medic?

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.450
Neither of them.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:36.110
We're supposed to focus on moving forward.

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:39.980
There should be a support truck, at least.

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:40.920
They could pick her up...

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:41.990
Wait!

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:43.870
I can still fight.

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:45.500
Don't push it.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.390
Really! I'll be fine!

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:48.370
Right, Stella?

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.840
The truck will be here soon.

00:10:58.310 --> 00:10:59.880
Stella?

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:02.940
Guess she doesn't want you holding us back.

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:04.230
That's mean!

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:06.080
I can still fight, really!

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:08.060
Sounds fine to me.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:10.840
If she says she can do it...

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:14.400
And we can always replace you if you die.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:15.140
Hey!

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:17.280
You're such a jerk! Ow...

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:17.280
Hey, now!

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:20.280
All right.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:21.530
Go on, we'll catch up.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:37.230
Um... thank you.

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:40.480
I'm sorry for the trouble.

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:46.610
So... you know medical stuff, huh?

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:51.840
I've looked after my share 
of injury-prone types.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:54.440
I guess you would. 
On battlefields and such...

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:56.320
More or less.

00:11:57.740 --> 00:12:01.680
Um... why did you join our squad?

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:02.700
How long has it been?

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:05.300
Since you joined this squad.

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:08.560
Two years now.

00:12:09.070 --> 00:12:12.510
Stella and I are the only ones 
who've been here from the start.

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:16.580
Huey transferred from 
another squad soon after,

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:18.890
but he was just as green as we were.

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:23.330
We received a lot of mockery and ridicule.

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:26.990
Did the others all die in battle?

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:28.630
Yes...

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:30.600
We went through a couple of replacements

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.960
before Warrant Officers 
Break and Pierce joined.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:35.020
I see.

00:12:36.260 --> 00:12:40.240
But... I'm really surprised 
I've lasted this long.

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:41.990
I owe it all to Stella.

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:46.970
You seem to place a lot of trust in her.

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:48.110
I do.

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:50.240
She's saved me time and time again.

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:55.750
Remember when that borderland 
unit started a coup d'etat?

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:01.650
Putting them down was harder 
than anyone expected.

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:04.130
They'd dug in deep with 
an all-out resistance.

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:06.890
In the end, both sides ran out of ammo,

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.190
and we had to fight hand-to-hand...

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:20.620
By that point, I was losing 
my will to fight back...

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:28.280
Lily!

00:13:29.730 --> 00:13:31.720
Stella had run out of ammo, too.

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:32.870
She had just one option left...

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:45.910
It really surprised me.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:49.450
That calm and cool Stella 
charged right into danger...

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.730
All to save me.

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:57.000
She's always been that way, then?

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:57.770
What way?

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:00.140
I just can't get a handle on her.

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.510
She's always smiling that artificial smile...

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:10.530
Have you ever seen one from her? 
A genuine, heartfelt smile?

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.230
Good question...

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:19.890
What is it?

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:21.540
<i>We've made it to the bridge.</i>

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:24.690
<i>We'll wait here for the 
other squads to arrive.</i>

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:27.330
Understood. I'm on my way now.

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:29.680
I'll leave it up to you.

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.050
If you don't think you'll 
hold us back, come along.

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:34.250
Yes, sir.

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:35.390
W-Wait...

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:41.620
Well... I feel like I said 
more than I meant to.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:44.820
You're a good listener, Commander.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:47.280
I'm used to dealing with kids, that's all.

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:48.530
Kids?

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:07.920
We'll push through the forest as a group, 
rushing our target from behind.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:12.800
I expect to find at least a 
few sentries in the forest.

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:17.220
If we end up in a firefight, 
the priority is for at least one squad...

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:20.300
at least one machine to reach the target.

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:21.310
That's all.

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:50.340
Petty Officer Fourier!

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:51.950
Spread out!

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.800
Our squad will draw fire.

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:00.090
You keep going!

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:01.070
Roger that! Thanks!

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:03.110
I'll head for the Order model!

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:04.930
Aja, Upton, follow me!

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:06.770
Guy, Eugen, stay here!

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.010
Roger that!

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:13.010
There's more ahead!

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:15.070
<i>We'll handle them! Come on!</i>

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:15.660
Roger that!

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:17.600
Keep going, Craighton!

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:18.490
Roger!

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:23.940
Got one!

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:25.950
<i>Same here! But...</i>

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:27.030
What's wrong?

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:28.630
<i>I've lost contact with our allies!</i>

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:29.490
What?

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:31.840
That one again...

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:47.900
Hurry it up, Pierce!

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:53.210
Okay, that's two down!

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:55.030
<i>Buerger... Squad...</i>

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:57.510
<i>Buerger Squad, do you read me?</i>

00:16:57.900 --> 00:16:58.640
That you, Guy?

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.380
<i>Eugen's down.</i>

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:03.160
<i>The rest of us were disabled...</i>

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:05.080
<i>by this one damned machine!</i>

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:06.620
He's down?

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:08.540
Wait, are you telling me Eugen's dead?!

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:09.660
Keep going!

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:11.300
Huey, Break, Pierce!

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:12.630
Don't worry about me!

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.190
More reinforcements?!

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:21.470
Huey, go on ahead!

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:22.550
Roger that!

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:29.610
Guy!

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:31.480
Huey...

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:32.920
Is that the one?!

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:34.350
Be... careful.

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:35.900
That thing's... fast!

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:48.830
D-Damn it!

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:20.200
Stella!

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:35.830
<i>Lily!</i>

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:48.480
You won't hit me with wild fire like that!

00:19:04.570 --> 00:19:05.580
It's broken?!

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:13.290
Take this!

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:25.930
<i>Don't move, Lily!</i>

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:35.360
Enough.

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:37.610
Don't bother chasing it.

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:42.820
Thank you, Lily.

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:46.240
<i>I didn't manage to take it out, though.</i>

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.340
The way you did back then...

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:50.410
<i>"Back then"?</i>

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:52.950
Never mind.

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:57.100
<i>Looks like you're totally grounded this time.</i>

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:59.420
You looked way worse than I did.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:00.290
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:02.930
Any left?

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:04.000
We cleared them up.

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:06.640
But the Hirsch Squad took 
major damage all around.

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:08.940
They lost a member, too.

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:11.240
Figures.

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:14.400
Stuck-up bastard, telling <i>me</i> not to die...

00:20:17.340 --> 00:20:21.030
But what can you do but laugh? 
It happens over and over...

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:28.710
The flare!

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:33.670
Looks like the Schaff Squad found their base.

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:37.030
They'll begin the main 
assault soon. Let's go.

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:41.080
Lily, you'll wait for the 
support truck this time, right?

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:42.500
Yes, sir.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:47.720
Your boosters are out, too. 
Can you still fight?

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:48.900
You bet.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:50.930
Walking or crawling, I'll be there.

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:52.720
Hey, no worries.

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:55.690
We can always replace you if you die!

00:20:56.010 --> 00:20:59.440
Telling someone that just improves 
their survival odds, y'know.

00:21:01.680 --> 00:21:05.670
Okay, we'll attack the enemy from 
behind to throw them off balance.

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:06.510
Let's go!

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:07.950
<i>Roger that!</i>

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:16.330
<i>Back then...</i>

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:19.060
Lily!

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:26.220
Lily!

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:31.220
Lily!

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:46.250
<i>I think that I saw it.</i>

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:50.490
<i>Stella's genuine, heartfelt smile...</i>

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:40.350
<b><i>The Crossroads of Fate</i></b>
